# Deliberately NO Git LFS in this repository.
#
# The upstream SONIC tree ships runner/.gitattributes routing *.a, *.so*, *.onnx,
# *.pkl and *.csv through LFS. That file is removed here on purpose. This bundle
# exists to be copied onto a machine and run, and an LFS clone on a host without
# git-lfs installed silently yields pointer files instead of libunitree_sdk2.a,
# libddsc.so and the two policies -- which surfaces much later as a link error or
# an ONNX parse failure that says nothing about LFS.
#
# Everything is a plain git object. `git clone` is enough. The two 55 MB ONNX
# files draw a GitHub size warning; that is the intended trade.
#
# `-filter` is the whole no-LFS lever, and it is the only attribute set here.
# This line used to read `* -filter -diff -merge`, which also turned off diffing
# and three-way merging for every path in the tree. The cost was not theoretical:
# every commit in this history renders as "Binary files a/x and b/x differ" with
# no hunks and no insertion count, so no change to a shell script or a document
# could be reviewed from the log, and any branch that touched the same text file
# as another had to be resolved by hand. Neither was ever the point -- LFS routing
# is `filter`, and git's own NUL-byte detection already treats the .onnx, .a,
# .so, .mp4 and .pkl payloads as binary for diff and merge without being told.
# Leave diff and merge to that detection; do not re-broaden this line.
* -filter
